 "brief": "The Gaza conflict is inflicting psychological tolls on Israel's military institution beyond battlefield casualties, Shehab Wire reported. Costs are accumulating within the armed forces themselves in ways less visible than combat losses but increasingly apparent over time as the campaign continues.\n\nStrain within the military reflects pressures distinct from conventional war metrics. Personnel face mounting psychological burdens that differ markedly from territorial gains or announced enemy losses. The psychological impact represents a secondary but growing dimension of the conflict's toll on Israeli forces, one that becomes more pronounced as operations extend across months of fighting.",
